"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. The project was introduced with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The budget was later adjusted to $550,000 to accommodate unforeseen expenses and the integration of real-time analytics. The project has progressed through several phases: the design phase was completed, leading to the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The team has expanded multiple times, adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, as well as specific hires like Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Strategic partnerships have been established, including a collaboration with TechInnovate for AI research. Significant progress has been made in phase two, specifically a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is currently being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
